<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robertians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Robertians were a Frankish noble family named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-strong">Robert the Strong</a>, who defended the lands between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> in the 860s. His sons Odo and Robert I became kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-francia">West Francia</a>, rivalling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingians</a>, and his descendant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-capet">Hugh Capet</a> took the throne in 987, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capetian-dynasty">Capetian dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robertians.jpg" alt="Robertians" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dafne07 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carolingis_i_robertians.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
